1
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:17,220
This is the third video presentation for the Case Animal and Plant Biotechnology course.
这是 CASE 动植物生物技术课程的第三个视频演示。

2
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:21,220
As you view this video, be sure to make notes of important information.
观看本视频时，请务必记下重要信息。

3
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:27,220
Feel free to pause, repeat, and resume the video whenever necessary.
必要时可以随时暂停、重播和继续播放视频。

4
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:32,220
Conducting Background Research, Lesson 2.2, Genetic Transformers
开展背景研究，第 2.2 课，基因转化者

5
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:39,220
Your teacher recently introduced Project 224 Rooted in Research and the related evaluation rubric.
你的老师最近介绍了项目 2.2.4“扎根研究”及相关的评分标准。

6
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:44,220
This presentation provides additional directions pertaining to your research paper.
本演示提供有关你的研究论文的补充说明。

7
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,220
Background research is important to identify what is already known about a topic.
背景研究对于确定某个主题已有哪些已知内容非常重要。

8
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:53,220
Formal writing improves communications about the topic.
规范的写作能改善关于该主题的交流。

9
00:00:53,220 --> 00:01:04,700
You should select one specific crop or plant that has been modified by Agrobacterium Tumifaciens to study.
你应该选择一种经根癌农杆菌改造过的具体作物或植物作为研究对象。

10
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:09,700
You will need to narrow your research focus once you determine your interests.
一旦确定了自己的兴趣所在，你就需要缩小研究重点。

11
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:17,920
A thesis forms the structure and organization of a research paper.
论点构成了研究论文的结构和组织框架。

12
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:24,920
A well-written thesis statement should be included in the introduction of the paper and guide the main points that follow.
论文的引言部分应包含一个精心撰写的论点陈述，并由它引领后续的要点。

13
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:30,920
Thesis statements are generally revised and edited as research progresses and the paper is drafted.
随着研究的推进和论文初稿的撰写，论点陈述通常会被修改和编辑。

14
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:40,760
It is okay, even expected, that the thesis statement evolves as the paper does.
论点陈述随着论文的发展而演变是可以的，甚至是意料之中的。

15
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:46,760
A research outline improves organization and clarity as you progress through the research process.
研究提纲能在你推进研究过程时提高条理性和清晰度。

16
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:50,760
Use the outline as a sort of roadmap to complete your paper.
把提纲当作一种路线图来完成你的论文。

17
00:01:50,760 --> 00:02:02,730
Developing an annotated bibliography helps organize your research and determine where to look for facts when compiling your paper.
编写一份带注释的参考文献目录，有助于整理你的研究，并在撰写论文时确定到哪里查找事实依据。

18
00:02:02,730 --> 00:02:08,730
An alternative to completing an annotated bibliography is the use of source cards and note cards.
除了编写带注释的参考文献目录，另一种方法是使用来源卡片和笔记卡片。

19
00:02:08,730 --> 00:02:14,730
If you choose this route, be sure to research the correct use of them and submit it on the due date.
如果你选择这种方式，一定要查明它们的正确用法，并在截止日期前提交。

20
00:02:14,730 --> 00:02:27,430
References used for research should come from credible sources such as research journals, texts, and government or university publications.
研究所用的参考资料应来自可信的来源，例如学术期刊、教科书以及政府或大学的出版物。

21
00:02:27,430 --> 00:02:34,430
Open source sites such as Winkipedia should not be used since anyone can add or change information at any time.
不应使用维基百科这类开放来源网站，因为任何人都可以随时添加或修改信息。

22
00:02:34,430 --> 00:02:41,430
However, open source sites can serve as a starting point to begin gathering additional sources or providing an overview for you.
不过，开放来源网站可以作为一个起点，用来开始收集其他资料，或为你提供概况。

23
00:02:41,430 --> 00:02:48,430
All sources referred to and or cited should be included in the works cited in correct APA format.
所有参考和／或引用的资料都应按照正确的 APA 格式列入引用文献中。

24
00:02:48,430 --> 00:02:58,300
Plagiarism may be intentional or unintentional, but neither is ethical or condoned by the scientific community.
剽窃可能是有意的，也可能是无意的，但两者都不道德，也不被科学界所容忍。

25
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:06,300
To preclude plagiarism, in-paper citations and a works cited section will help a reader understand sources of information and quotations.
为了避免剽窃，文中引注和引用文献部分能帮助读者了解信息和引文的来源。

26
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:16,500
Shorter quotes are written inside quotation marks. Longer quotes are inserted in a block.
较短的引文写在引号内。较长的引文以独立段落的形式插入。

27
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:22,500
Either way, the author, year, and page reference must be included in a paragraph at the end.
无论哪种方式，都必须在末尾的括注中注明作者、年份和页码。

28
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:28,500
Quoting sources in APA format may be intimidating at first, but you have many references to help you.
用 APA 格式引用资料起初可能会让人望而生畏，但你有很多参考资料可以借助。

29
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:32,500
One such reference is the Purdue Online Writing Lab.
其中之一就是普渡大学在线写作实验室。

30
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:43,050
Scientific writing is completed in third-person form. Formal writing uses complete words and phrasing.
科学写作采用第三人称。规范写作使用完整的词语和措辞。

31
00:03:43,050 --> 00:03:47,050
Italicized font is used for scientific names.
学名使用斜体字。

32
00:03:47,050 --> 00:03:57,950
Once early drafts have been completed, editing and revision catch errors, typos, and mistakes in writing.
完成初稿后，通过编辑和修改找出写作中的错误、错别字和失误。

33
00:03:57,950 --> 00:04:04,950
Complete readings of the paper will determine if the objectives have been reached and whether or not the paper is organized.
完整地通读论文，可以确定是否达到了目标，以及论文是否条理清晰。

34
00:04:04,950 --> 00:04:16,210
As a review, mark or highlight three key points in your notes that are important to remember from this presentation.
作为复习，请在笔记中标记或突出显示本演示中需要记住的三个要点。

35
00:04:16,210 --> 00:04:20,210
List two ideas or concepts that relate to previous knowledge.
列出两个与已有知识相关的观点或概念。

36
00:04:20,210 --> 00:04:26,210
List any questions you have about this topic. Discuss these questions with your instructor.
列出你对这个主题的任何疑问。与你的老师讨论这些问题。

37
00:04:26,210 --> 00:04:32,210
Keep any notes you have from this presentation organized and available for use throughout the course.
把你在本演示中做的所有笔记整理好，以便在整个课程中随时使用。

38
00:04:32,210 --> 00:04:40,210
Throughout the next few weeks, you will conduct research, compile an annotated bibliography, and write a first draft of a research paper.
在接下来的几周里，你将开展研究，编写一份带注释的参考文献目录，并撰写研究论文的初稿。

39
00:04:40,210 --> 00:04:48,210
Then, you and a partner will conduct peer reviews on each other's papers. Your teacher will provide guidance throughout the process.
然后，你和一位搭档将互相评审对方的论文。你的老师会在整个过程中提供指导。
